# Git

Canonical for this repo **and** for `mcp-execution-engine` / `mcp-gateway`. Those repos point here — do not fork a second copy of these habits.

## When

- Do **not** commit, push, or open a PR unless the human asks.
- Working-tree **inspection** (branch, dirty files) is fine. Do not stash, checkout, create, rename, or push branches unless asked.

## Three repos

A “please commit”, “please commit and push”, or similar ask is **all three** checkouts (`website`, `mcp-execution-engine`, `mcp-gateway`) — not only the repo in focus. Commit (and push, if asked) in every repo that has a change. Skip a clean tree.

## Signing

Commits are signed. The human confirms with a fingerprint; that can take a few seconds. Wait for the prompt (do not treat a short delay as failure). Do not retry in a tight loop, skip signing, or abandon the commit because the signer has not answered yet.

## Commit messages

One short line. Name the thing that shipped. No conventional-commit prefix (`feat:`, `fix:`), no body, no invented PR numbers (`#52` is added on merge).

Match `git log --oneline` on the repo you are committing:

```
EIP-7843 Exploration
EIP-8037 MCP + new run_transaction tool
Eip-7843 Comic + Video
Twitter Refinement
Small fix
```

- EIP work: `EIP-NNNN` + artifact (`Exploration`, `MCP`, `Comic + Video`).
- Otherwise a two-to-five-word Title Case label (`Launch Strategy`, `CI fix`).
- If unsure, copy the nearest recent subject on that repo — do not write a paragraph.
